<title>USA: GOLF-LEADING SCORES AT DORAL AFTER RAIN-HIT SECOND ROUND.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SCORES AT DORAL AFTER RAIN-HIT SECOND ROUND.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores from the $1.8</p>
<p>million Doral-Ryder Open at Doral Resort &amp; Spa (Blue course,</p>
<p>6,939 yards, par 72) after the rain-suspended second round on</p>
<p>Friday with 15 players yet to complete the round Saturday</p>
<p>morning (players U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>134 Greg Norman (Australia) 66 68, David Duval 68 66</p>
<p>135 Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 68 67</p>
<p>136 Steve Elkington (Australia) 70 66  </p>
<p>137 Phil Mickelson 69 68, Billy Mayfair 70 67, Bob Tway 66 71</p>
<p>138 Jesper Parnevik (Sweden) 72 66, Larry Nelson 72 66, Colin</p>
<p>Montgomerie 69 69, Robert Damron 72 66, Chris Perry 71 67,</p>
<p>Ronnie Black 67 71, Sandy Lyle (Britain) 67 71  </p>
<p>139 Tommy Tolles 68 71, Billy Andrade 68 71, Nick Faldo</p>
<p>(Britain) 71 68, Brad Bryant 69 70, Scott Gump 71 68, Ted</p>
<p>Tryba 70 69, Jay Haas 67 72, Bruce Lietzke 69 70</p>
<p>Add non-U.S. players</p>
<p>140 Craig Parry (Australia) 70 70, Fulton Allem (South</p>
<p>Africa) 70 70, Grant Waite (New Zealand) 72 68</p>
<p>142 Naomichi &quot;Joe&quot; Ozaki (Japan) 70 72  </p>
<p>144 Vijay Singh (Fiji) 72 72  </p>
<p>145 Ernie Els (South Africa) 73 72</p>
</text>
